</p></sec></body><back><glossary><title>Abbreviations</title><def-list><def-item><term>C|ShS|<sub>L</sub></term><def><p id="Par12">Cumulated absolute lateral shear strain magnitude</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>ES</term><def><p id="Par13">Erector spinae</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>ICC</term><def><p id="Par14">Intraclass coefficient correlation</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>Max|ShS|<sub>L</sub></term><def><p id="Par15">Maximum absolute lateral shear strain</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>NSLBP</term><def><p id="Par16">Nonspecific low back pain</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>RF</term><def><p id="Par17">Radiofrequency</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>ROI</term><def><p id="Par18">Region of interest</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>SD</term><def><p id="Par19">Standard deviation</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>ShS</term><def><p id="Par20">Shear strain</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>TLF</term><def><p id="Par21">Thoracolumbar fascia</p></def></def-item></def-list></glossary><fn-group><fn><p><bold>Publisher&#x02019;s Note</bold> Springer Nature remains neutral with regard to jurisdictional claims in published maps and institutional affiliations.</p></fn></fn-group><sec><title>Supplementary information</title><p>The online version contains supplementary material available at 10.1186/s13244-024-01895-2.</p></sec><ack><title>Acknowledgements</title><p>We want to thank Mr. Casey Bourdeau-Caporuscio for his valuable coordination in conducting this study. We are also grateful to Dr. Hiroshi Nagai (United Engineering, Tokyo, Japan) for providing insightful advice on implementing the electrical circuit during the development of the Force Sensor System.</p></ack><notes notes-type="author-contribution"><title>Author contributions</title><p>N.T. designed the study, performed the ultrasound exams, massage, and sham techniques, analyzed and interpreted the imaging and clinical data, and drafted the manuscript. M.-H.R.-C. interpreted imaging data and performed statistical analysis. B.C. assisted with the design of the study and the technical aspects of the ultrasound exams. S.D. analyzed imaging and clinical data. A.A. analyzed imaging and clinical data. A.B. conceived and designed the study and recruited participants. N.G. conceived and designed the study and interpreted imaging and clinical data. G.C. conceived and designed the study and interpreted imaging data. N.J.B. conceived and designed the study, recruited participants, performed the ultrasound exams, analyzed imaging and clinical data, and wrote the final manuscript. All authors read and approved the final version of the manuscript.</p></notes><notes notes-type="funding-information"><title>Funding</title><p>This study was funded by the Massage Therapy Research Fund (MTRF 2019-2020) awarded to N.J.B. and N.G., and the Fonds de recherche du Qu&#x000e9;bec Soci&#x000e9;t&#x000e9; et Culture (FRQSC, Audace program #284121) awarded to N.J.B. and G.C. N.J.B. was supported by a research scholarship from the Fonds de Recherche du Qu&#x000e9;bec&#x02014;Sant&#x000e9; (FRQ-S) and the Fondation de l&#x02019;Association des Radiologistes du Qu&#x000e9;bec (FRQS-ARQ #266408). N.T. was supported by a doctoral scholarship from the Fonds de Recherche du Qu&#x000e9;bec&#x02014;Nature et Technologies (FRQNT #316861). The funding bodies had no role in the design of the study, collection, analysis, and interpretation of data, nor in writing the manuscript.</p></notes><notes notes-type="data-availability"><title>Data availability</title><p>Upon request, the corresponding author can provide access to datasets analyzed in this study.</p></notes><notes><title>Declarations</title><notes id="FPar1"><title>Ethics approval and consent to participate</title><p id="Par57">The Centre Hospitalier de l&#x02019;Universit&#x000e9; de Montr&#x000e9;al Ethics Committee approved the study (CE 19.358), and all participants signed informed consent.</p></notes><notes id="FPar2"><title>Consent for publication</title><p id="Par58">Each participant provided informed consent, which included permission to use anonymized personal data for publication.</p></notes><notes id="FPar3" notes-type="COI-statement"><title>Competing interests</title><p id="Par59">N.T. is a massage therapist certified by the F&#x000e9;d&#x000e9;ration qu&#x000e9;b&#x000e9;coise des massoth&#x000e9;rapeutes agr&#x000e9;&#x000e9;s (FQM) and the CEO and Chief Therapist of Atelier Tomita Inc., which provides therapeutic massage services in Quebec. The other authors declare that they have no competing interests.</p></notes></notes><ref-list id="Bib1"><title>References</title><ref id="CR1"><label>1.</label><citation-alternatives><element-citation id="ec-CR1" publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hoy</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>March</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Brooks</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The global burden of low back pain: estimates from the global burden of disease 2010 study</article-title><source>Ann Rheum Dis</source><year>2014</year><volume>73</volume><fpage>968</fpage><lpage>974</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/annrheumdis-2013-204428</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">24665116</pub-id>
